# Cursor Rules for KHI Next.js Project

## Project Overview

This is a Next.js 15 project with TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, and Turbopack for development.

## Tech Stack

- Next.js 15 with App Router
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS
- Turbopack (for dev mode)
- pnpm (package manager)

## Code Style

- Use TypeScript strict mode
- Follow Next.js best practices
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling
- Prefer functional components with hooks
- Use proper TypeScript types
- Follow ESLint rules

## File Structure

- `/src/app/` - App Router pages and layouts
- `/src/components/` - Reusable components
- `/src/lib/` - Utility functions and configurations
- `/src/types/` - TypeScript type definitions

## Development Guidelines

- Always write mobile-responsive code
- Avoid infinite loops in useEffect
- Check if packages are already available before installing
- Use proper error handling
- Follow accessibility best practices
- Always implement best practices in code
- Never create big jsx files, instead create small components and use them in parent files
- If you find a function being used in multiple places, think about making hook to reuse
- Always use Nextjs Image component to show images and make sure it's optimized with lazyloading, loading skeleton and container

## Commands

- `pnpm dev` - Start development server with Turbopack
- `pnpm build` - Build for production
- `pnpm start` - Start production server
- `pnpm lint` - Run ESLint
